        "title": "Industrial Mycology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nTHE SUPPLY PROBLEM (1941):\n  Fleming's P. notatum: produced ~2 units/mL in culture\n  Growing Penicillium in flasks: labor-intensive; tiny yield\n  WWII demand: Allied forces needed penicillin at industrial scale\n  US Army + pharmaceutical companies + USDA: crash program 1941–1945"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-INDUSTRIAL-MYCOLOGY.md#013",
      "path": [
        "09-INDUSTRIAL-MYCOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
