        "root_concepts": "[industrial, mycology]",
        "section": "mycology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Industrial Mycology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THE PEORIA CANTALOUPE:\n  USDA Northern Regional Research Laboratory, Peoria, Illinois\n  Mary Hunt (\"Mouldy Mary\"): tasked with finding better Penicillium strains\n    from any local source of moldy material\n  1943: A moldy cantaloupe from a Peoria market\n  Strain: Penicillium chrysogenum (now reclassified P. rubens)\n  Yield: ~100 units/mL (vs. 2 units/mL from Fleming's strain)\n    → 50× improvement from a piece of rotten fruit"
    }
